WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.611
Aladdin was so happy!

2
00:00:16.612 --> 00:00:22.913
He was married to his beautiful princess and lived in his grand palace.

3
00:00:22.914 --> 00:00:27.337
Aladdin had forgotten about the evil magician.

4
00:00:27.338 --> 00:00:32.647
But Magrib had not forgotten about the lamp, my young friends.

5
00:00:32.648 --> 00:00:38.137
Oh no. Magrib never stopped thinking about it.

6
00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:44.683
In fact, he had used a spell to create a blue crystal ball that could find anything.

7
00:00:44.684 --> 00:00:48.987
He hoped to see the magic lamp through the mist in the ball.

8
00:00:48.988 --> 00:00:53.074
"Oh, I can see inside the enchanted treasury!"

9
00:00:53.075 --> 00:00:56.323
he said, staring into the ball.

10
00:00:56.324 --> 00:01:00.999
"Hmmm—but where is the lamp?"

11
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:05.532
He moved around the crystal ball, hoping to get a better view.

12
00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:07.677
"I don't see the lamp.

13
00:01:07.678 --> 00:01:09.895
I don't see that boy either.

14
00:01:09.896 --> 00:01:12.766
He should be lying there dead."

15
00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:16.362
Magrib paced up and down his room.

16
00:01:16.363 --> 00:01:23.042
Then he pressed his bony hands against the sides of the crystal ball.

17
00:01:23.043 --> 00:01:27.779
"Show me where Aladdin is!" demanded the magician.

18
00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.267
He looked deep into the mist again.

19
00:01:31.268 --> 00:01:34.651
"What's this?" he hissed.

20
00:01:34.652 --> 00:01:36.563
His face grew dark.

21
00:01:36.564 --> 00:01:40.452
His pale eyes flashed.

22
00:01:40.453 --> 00:01:46.650
Magrib saw Aladdin in a palace, not dead in the enchanted treasury.

23
00:01:46.651 --> 00:01:52.222
He was dressed in fine clothes and walking with a beautiful woman.

24
00:01:52.223 --> 00:01:55.921
"He is alive," cried Magrib.

25
00:01:55.922 --> 00:01:57.658
"He is rich!"

26
00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:00.297
He looked into the ball again.

27
00:02:00.298 --> 00:02:04.233
"And he has married a princess!"

28
00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:10.964
That day, before the sun set, the magician was on his way back to Aladdin's home.

29
00:02:10.965 --> 00:02:14.439
"I'll find him again!" he said.

30
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:18.113
"And this time, I'll get the lamp!"

31
00:02:18.114 --> 00:02:26.653
When Magrib arrived in Aladdin's city, everyone he passed was talking about Aladdin's palace.

32
00:02:26.654 --> 00:02:30.808
"It's grander than the sultan's," one man said.

33
00:02:30.809 --> 00:02:33.681
"Wait until you see it!"

34
00:02:33.682 --> 00:02:35.803
"It is the magic of the lamp!"

35
00:02:35.804 --> 00:02:38.742
Magrib growled to himself.

36
00:02:38.743 --> 00:02:40.419
He turned to the man.

37
00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:43.806
"Where is his palace?"

38
00:02:43.807 --> 00:02:47.504
The man pointed the way, and then added,

39
00:02:47.505 --> 00:02:49.470
"But Aladdin's not home.

40
00:02:49.471 --> 00:02:52.434
He's away hunting for a week."

41
00:02:52.435 --> 00:02:57.239
When the wicked Magrib heard this, he thought of a plan.

42
00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:02.779
The next day, he went and bought a dozen new lamps.

43
00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:06.469
They looked exactly like the magic lamp.

44
00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:11.526
Magrib dressed in rags and carried the lamps through the streets.

45
00:03:11.527 --> 00:03:16.464
"Who will trade an old lamp for a new lamp?" he called out.

46
00:03:16.465 --> 00:03:19.793
People shook their heads when they heard him.

47
00:03:19.794 --> 00:03:24.153
"New for old?" a woman laughed.

48
00:03:24.154 --> 00:03:28.230
"Whoever heard of such a silly trade?"

49
00:03:28.231 --> 00:03:31.652
Magrib did not pay any attention.

50
00:03:31.653 --> 00:03:36.561
He went up and down the streets, shouting louder and louder,

51
00:03:36.562 --> 00:03:40.516
"Who will trade an old lamp for a new one?"

52
00:03:40.517 --> 00:03:45.646
Slowly, he made his way to Aladdin's palace.

53
00:03:45.647 --> 00:03:50.914
Princess Badra and her attendants sat by an open window in the palace.

54
00:03:50.915 --> 00:03:56.337
They were eating fruit sherbets and sewing pretty scarves with silk thread.

55
00:03:56.338 --> 00:04:00.315
"What is that noise?" asked Princess Badra.

56
00:04:00.316 --> 00:04:03.315
"Who is shouting?"

57
00:04:03.316 --> 00:04:06.630
One of her attendants ran to the window.

58
00:04:06.631 --> 00:04:12.131
"Who will trade an old lamp for a new lamp?" called Magrib.

59
00:04:12.132 --> 00:04:16.623
The attendant at the window started laughing.

60
00:04:16.624 --> 00:04:22.051
"What are you laughing about, girl?" asked the princess.

61
00:04:22.052 --> 00:04:26.022
"A madman!" cried the attendant.

62
00:04:26.023 --> 00:04:29.903
"He wants to trade his new lamps for old ones!"

63
00:04:29.904 --> 00:04:33.835
When Princess Badra heard this, she jumped up.

64
00:04:33.836 --> 00:04:37.123
"We have an old brass lamp," she said.

65
00:04:37.124 --> 00:04:39.229
"I'll go and get it."

66
00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:43.408
Princess Badra ran out of the room.

67
00:04:43.409 --> 00:04:48.493
When she returned, she was carrying Aladdin's wonderful lamp.

68
00:04:48.494 --> 00:04:51.701
"Here," she said to a servant.

69
00:04:51.702 --> 00:04:55.191
"Take this dirty, old lamp downstairs.

70
00:04:55.192 --> 00:04:58.604
Let's see if that man is telling the truth.

71
00:04:58.605 --> 00:05:05.648
Here is an old lamp for a new one!"
